{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["Some say that the number seventy is the total count, for they were sixty-nine, and this commentator erred, for we find \"all the souls of his sons and his daughters\" are thirty-three, yet they are thirty-two. And in the derash, that Jochebed was born between the walls — this too is astonishing: why did Scripture not mention the wonder done with her, that she bore Moses and she was 130 years old? And why did it mention the matter of Sarah, who was ninety? And this trouble is not enough for us, for paytanim composed piyyutim on the day of Simḥat Torah: \"Jochebed my mother, after be comforted,\" and she was 250 years old, and that her brother lived thus and thus many years — by way of aggadah or the words of an individual. And the correct view in my eyes is that Jacob is included in the count, and from him it begins, as if it said: all the souls of his sons and his daughters together with his own soul are thirty-three. And the proof for this is that it says at the beginning \"Jacob and his sons.\" And if a disputant should object and say: but it is written, \"and all the souls who went out of Jacob's thigh were seventy souls\" — know that Scripture did not trouble to exclude one from the seventy, just as it said \"who were born to him in Paddan-aram\" (Genesis 35:26), yet Benjamin was not born to him there. For also in this passage there are two witnesses: the first, that it said, \"And these are the names of the children of Israel who came to Egypt: Jacob and his sons\" (Genesis 46:8) — and behold it counted Jacob among the children of Israel, for Scripture went only after the majority. And the second witness: \"all the souls of the house of Jacob who came to Egypt were seventy\" (Genesis 46:27) — and Manasseh and Ephraim did not come to Egypt, for he was there and there they were born. And after it: \"with seventy souls your fathers went down to Egypt\" (Deuteronomy 10:22) — and these two did not go down. This too is a witness that Jacob enters the count, for he has a soul and he is the principal."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {0 "I read והיא בת ר\"נ as 250 years, following the sense of the piyyut parody Ibn Ezra is quoting; the exact reference is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:15.421671002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}